Census data is invaluable for research regarding the changing
demographics of the American population.  To make this analysis
easier, we have just created three new packages (complete product
listing below):
 
* Census 2000 - designed for the person who wants all of the
current 2000 data.

* Census Reference - created for the researcher who wants the
entire 2000 Census data AND Long Form (SF3) data for 1970, 1980
and 1990.  

* Census Time Series Research - ideal for the researcher/analyst
who needs access to as much data as possible - especially those
who want to do time series analysis.  It includes two products
that convert data from previous censuses (1970, 1980, or 1990) to
the 2000 boundaries.  This allows for apples-to-apples comparison
of changes to 2000.  

Our Census 2000 Package includes all of our CensusCD 2000
products:
* Long Form
* Long Form Profile
* Short Form
* Short Form Blocks
* Redistricting
* Redistricting Blocks

This package has a total of 12 disks.  The price for all of these
products if purchased separately is $3,175. As a bundled package
it is only $1,595 for the country or $795 for a single state.

The Census Reference Package has ALL of our CensusCD 2000 products
AND all of our Long Form products for the previous decades.  It
includes 
* Entire Census 2000 Package PLUS
* CensusCD 1970
* CensusCD 1980
* CensusCD 1990

This reference set provides all of the basic Census data available
for the four censuses (1970-2000).  The price for all of these
products, if purchased separately would be $5,865 but as a bundled
package it is only $2,995 for the nation or $1,495 for a single
state.

The Census Research Time Series Package includes ALL of our
census-based products in one bundle.  It is our most comprehensive
package and includes:

* Entire CensusCD 2000 Package 
* Census Reference packages PLUS 
* Neighborhood Change Database (1970-2000 data normalized to the
2000 tract boundaries)
* CensusCD 1990 in 2000 Boundaries (the entire 1990 Long Form in 
all of the various 2000 LF boundaries)

With these products the researcher can analyze what a given area
looked like at the time of the census (Reference Package) AND also
compare a defined, specific area over time without having to
account for the geographic changes that have taken place with
redistricting.  For a complete description of our normalizing
procedures please check the variables page of the NCDB listing on
our website http://www.censusdata1.com

This package includes 17 disks covering 11 different products. The
price for all of these products if purchased separately would be
$9,150, but as a bundled package it is only $3,995.

Note: there is no 10% discount available - these packages already
include a 50% discount.  Also all of our products are also
available for Network usage - call for pricing.

All of our census-based products come with built-in mapping
capabilities.  With a few quick keystrokes you can generate full
blown maps or tables.  You can extract data as dbf, ASCII, shape
or mid/mif files and use them as input files for other programs
e.g. statistical (SAS, SPSS), database (Access, Oracle),
spreadsheet (Excel, 1-2-3), and mapping (Arc View, MapInfo).

